# Every text file checks out with LF, on every platform, regardless of a
# contributor's own `core.autocrlf`. Windows CI checking this out with CRLF
# is what broke tests/no-terminal-in-home.test.ts: it reads App.tsx's own
# source and searches for a literal "\n", which a CRLF checkout never
# contains. `eol=lf` is the fix, not the test: any future test reading its
# own source text would have hit the same wall.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
